N1  - D1. Buildings are the major energy users and consume more than 30% of global energy usage [2], among which a significant proportion is used for heating, ventilation, and air-conditioning (HVAC) [3]. 
N1  - D2. The optimal design can reduce the EGN of 12.2% and the total system cost of 5.5%, compared to a base design case. 
N1  - D3. Optimization can decrease the 20-year LCC of the system by more than 10% in comparison to baseline design cases. 
N1  - D4. The COP of this hybrid GSHP optimized using the utility concept was 4.23, 8.74% higher than that optimized using the Taguchi method. 
N1  - D5. To solve soil temperature fluctuation, performance analysis for the first 10 years is important during the design. 17% decrease in total present value cost, 10% decrease in annual energy use, and a 7% increase in total initial cost as compared with the results from another study. 
N1  - D6. The GSHP in the hybrid system can usually meet more than 80% of the total annual heating and cooling demand of buildings through optimization. 
